{"id":"e1616e874e8eb33c","group":"58","path":"58/batch10/58-df-modular-curve.md","title":"Modular-Curve Orbit Presentation","display":"df-modular-curve — Modular-Curve Orbit Presentation","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-modular-curve","aliases":["58-df-modular-curve","Modular Curve"],"display":"df-modular-curve — Modular-Curve Orbit Presentation","depends_on":["[[../batch12/58-df-modular-group.md]]","[[../batch19/58-df-finite-index.md]]","[[../batch09/58-df-group.md]]","[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-modular-curve"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-modular-curve</span><span>Modular Curve</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-modular-curve — Modular-Curve Orbit Presentation"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"dbeb6e7ed5730d0f\" href=\"?note=dbeb6e7ed5730d0f\" title=\"../batch12/58-df-modular-group.md\">../batch12/58-df-modular-group.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"c27bfe92f372d3ac\" href=\"?note=c27bfe92f372d3ac\" title=\"../batch19/58-df-finite-index.md\">../batch19/58-df-finite-index.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"ed71f39f59370734\" href=\"?note=ed71f39f59370734\" title=\"../batch09/58-df-group.md\">../batch09/58-df-group.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb H=\\{z\\in\\mathbb C:\\operatorname{Im}(z)&gt;0\\}\">\\(\\mathbb H=\\{z\\in\\mathbb C:\\operatorname{Im}(z)&gt;0\\}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"Z^\\ast=\\mathbb H\\cup\\mathbb P^1(\\mathbb Q)\">\\(Z^\\ast=\\mathbb H\\cup\\mathbb P^1(\\mathbb Q)\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X_\\Gamma,Y_\\Gamma,\\Gamma,m,e,a\\in V\">\\(X_\\Gamma,Y_\\Gamma,\\Gamma,m,e,a\\in V\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"m\">\\(m\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"e\">\\(e\\)</span> are the supplied group operation and identity on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Gamma\">\\(\\Gamma\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"a:\\Gamma\\times Z^\\ast\\to Z^\\ast\">\\(a:\\Gamma\\times Z^\\ast\\to Z^\\ast\\)</span> is a supplied action preserving <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb H\">\\(\\mathbb H\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{FiniteIndex}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{FiniteIndex}_S\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Group}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Group}_S\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Function}\">\\(\\mathrm{Function}\\)</span> are from the cited dependencies.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ModularCurve}_S:V^6\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{ModularCurve}_S:V^6\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Cusps}_a\">\\(\\operatorname{Cusps}_a\\)</span> is the cusp-orbit set operation defined below.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}modular\\text{-}curve}\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{ModularCurve}_S(X_\\Gamma,Y_\\Gamma,\\Gamma,m,e,a)\\\\\n\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{FiniteIndex}_S(\\Gamma,PSL_2(\\mathbb Z))\n\\land\\mathrm{Group}_S(\\Gamma,m)\n\\land e\\in\\Gamma\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\forall\\gamma\\in\\Gamma\\;\n\\bigl(m(\\langle e,\\gamma\\rangle)=\\gamma\n\\land m(\\langle\\gamma,e\\rangle)=\\gamma\\bigr)\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\mathrm{Function}(a,\\Gamma\\times Z^\\ast,Z^\\ast)\n\\land\\forall z\\in Z^\\ast\\;(a(\\langle e,z\\rangle)=z)\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\forall\\gamma,\\delta\\in\\Gamma\\;\\forall z\\in Z^\\ast\\;\n\\bigl(\na(\\langle m(\\langle\\gamma,\\delta\\rangle),z\\rangle)\n=a(\\langle\\gamma,a(\\langle\\delta,z\\rangle)\\rangle)\n\\bigr)\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\forall\\gamma\\in\\Gamma\\;\\forall z\\in\\mathbb H\\;\n\\bigl(a(\\langle\\gamma,z\\rangle)\\in\\mathbb H\\bigr)\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land Y_\\Gamma=\n\\bigl\\{\\{a(\\langle\\gamma,z\\rangle):\\gamma\\in\\Gamma\\}:z\\in\\mathbb H\\bigr\\}\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land X_\\Gamma=\n\\bigl\\{\\{a(\\langle\\gamma,z\\rangle):\\gamma\\in\\Gamma\\}:z\\in Z^\\ast\\bigr\\}.\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}modular\\text{-}curve}\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{ModularCurve}_S(X_\\Gamma,Y_\\Gamma,\\Gamma,m,e,a)\\\\\n\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{FiniteIndex}_S(\\Gamma,PSL_2(\\mathbb Z))\n\\land\\mathrm{Group}_S(\\Gamma,m)\n\\land e\\in\\Gamma\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\forall\\gamma\\in\\Gamma\\;\n\\bigl(m(\\langle e,\\gamma\\rangle)=\\gamma\n\\land m(\\langle\\gamma,e\\rangle)=\\gamma\\bigr)\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\mathrm{Function}(a,\\Gamma\\times Z^\\ast,Z^\\ast)\n\\land\\forall z\\in Z^\\ast\\;(a(\\langle e,z\\rangle)=z)\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\forall\\gamma,\\delta\\in\\Gamma\\;\\forall z\\in Z^\\ast\\;\n\\bigl(\na(\\langle m(\\langle\\gamma,\\delta\\rangle),z\\rangle)\n=a(\\langle\\gamma,a(\\langle\\delta,z\\rangle)\\rangle)\n\\bigr)\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\forall\\gamma\\in\\Gamma\\;\\forall z\\in\\mathbb H\\;\n\\bigl(a(\\langle\\gamma,z\\rangle)\\in\\mathbb H\\bigr)\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land Y_\\Gamma=\n\\bigl\\{\\{a(\\langle\\gamma,z\\rangle):\\gamma\\in\\Gamma\\}:z\\in\\mathbb H\\bigr\\}\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land X_\\Gamma=\n\\bigl\\{\\{a(\\langle\\gamma,z\\rangle):\\gamma\\in\\Gamma\\}:z\\in Z^\\ast\\bigr\\}.\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}modular\\text{-}curve\\text{-}cusps}\\vdash\n\\operatorname{Cusps}_a(\\Gamma)\n\\coloneqq\n\\bigl\\{\\{a(\\langle\\gamma,c\\rangle):\\gamma\\in\\Gamma\\}:c\\in\\mathbb P^1(\\mathbb Q)\\bigr\\}.\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}modular\\text{-}curve\\text{-}cusps}\\vdash\n\\operatorname{Cusps}_a(\\Gamma)\n\\coloneqq\n\\bigl\\{\\{a(\\langle\\gamma,c\\rangle):\\gamma\\in\\Gamma\\}:c\\in\\mathbb P^1(\\mathbb Q)\\bigr\\}.\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The corrected finite-index predicate is <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{FiniteIndex}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{FiniteIndex}_S\\)</span>, not the nonexistent <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{FiniteIndexSubgroup}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{FiniteIndexSubgroup}_S\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>The quotient sets are explicit orbit sets for a set-coded action. Certifying that <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"a\">\\(a\\)</span> is the standard fractional-linear action is intentionally a separate presentation choice.</li>\n<li>Coarse Riemann-surface and compactification structures are downstream of this carrier-level orbit construction.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Diamond and Shurman, A First Course in Modular Forms</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch12/58-df-modular-group.md","status":"resolved","id":"dbeb6e7ed5730d0f","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch12/58-df-modular-group.md]]","embed":false},{